# fixes to clients already sitting on v1.0.0.1, then deliberately forced back to upstream's
# 1.0.0.1 the same day: the whole divergence existed for one day of debugging, and permanently
# carrying a TC-only version number costs more than the one-off "delete and reinstall" it saves.
# Consequence, by design: v1.0.0.1-TC13 is re-clobbered rather than superseded, so Dalamud offers
# no update and anyone already on v1.0.0.1 must delete and reinstall. Publishing therefore needs
